description: After any git commit in this repo, automatically push to origin
alwaysApply: true
---

# Auto push after commit

When the user asks you to create a git commit in this repository:

1. After a successful `git commit`, immediately run `git push -u origin HEAD` (or `git push` if upstream already tracks).
2. Do not ask for confirmation to push — the user has opted into auto-push for subsequent commits.
3. If push fails (network/auth), report the error; do not retry destructively or force-push.
4. Never `git push --force` to main/master unless the user explicitly requests it.
